[12.866446, "o", "Station geometry\r\n================\r\n\r\nFrame size: 160 x 120\r\nRate: 12 fps\r\nHorizontal scan row: y = 70 (top of frame is y = 0)\r\n\r\nDrive:\r\n\r\n    python3 /app/varnish/mill.pyc CLIP\r\n\r\nCLIP is an mp4 path. Success writes /app/inkwell/sheet.toml:\r\n\r\n    crossings = <integer>\r\n\r\nWorked sample: /app/shown.mp4 -> crossings = 3\r\n\r\nSimilar silhouettes that share the scan still count as separate when each\r\ncentroid completes top-to-bottom, including overlap or one body shading another.\r\n\r\nUnreadable CLIP: non-zero exit, do not write /app/inkwell/sheet.toml.\r\nExample unreadable path:\r\n\r\n    python3 /app/varnish/mill.pyc /tmp/no-such-fordwick.mp4\r\n\r\nFold blot, tether, spout, and the spanwell driver using the kiln notes.\r\n"]
[12.866788, "o", "\r\n--- KILN ---\r\n"]
[12.868251, "o", "Kiln card\r\n=========\r\n\r\nThe station mill is the folded snapshot named in /app/slipfold/SPAN.txt.\r\nIt is built from blot, tether, spout, and the spanwell driver under /app.\r\n\r\nThis directory holds the fold tools. Run the executable script here after\r\nediting those modules. Live pipeline files are not what the station executes.\r\n"]
[12.868455, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@0a311768df85:/app# "]
[13.004876, "i", "find /app -maxdepth 3 -type f -printf '%p\\n' | sort\n"]
